  "worked_solution": "First, notice that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly independent. \n\nThe closest vector to $x$ in the subspace spanned by ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace, which is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\,\u27f9\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following projection:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 12\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{32}[\\begin{aligned}12 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}22 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
